jabulanim kizi sits alongside the body  of his 19 year old daughter  her body was discovered after she was  washed away by flood waters in hernandez  outside the port city of durban  they still haven't found her sister  who's been missing for two days  what happened to our family is  devastating i've lost two of my  daughters my other daughter and wife are  in hospital and the worst part is that  we have not received any help from the  government the only help we have is from  the community  is leading the search for missing people  after heavy rain and mudslides  devastated this region of south africa  as they walk through the steep hills  that force the torrents of water through  the village  she says this is where the first body  was found at least five other people  from this community are missing  throughout ananda the destruction only  worsens roads and bridges have collapsed  cutting of people from main roads  there's no electricity or running water  here at least four homes have been  reduced to rubble  we heard people shouting my brother and  father tried to rescue them but by then  the houses were covered by water and the  tree collapsed on the houses we don't  know what happened to them people here  say they can't do much to find those who  are missing  while president sular mapos has visited  some of the flood-stricken areas and  offered government support this  community says there's not been any so  far  informal settlements have been severely  affected by the heavy rain and flooding  while the rain has slowed for now it's  expected to get worse people who escape  the first wave of flooding are worried  they'll not be as fortunate in the  coming days familia miller al jazeera  durban south africa
 

